course: dictionary
lesson: 7083
title: Paw
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. These are its context, and they leave clues. «Your dog is fast asleep on the rug, but its paws are paddling, its lips twitch and it gives tiny muffled woofs.» A dog that is asleep and paddling is probably moving its feet in a dream, so a paw must be a foot.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «its feet are paddling» instead of «its paws are paddling». It still makes sense, so feet is a good meaning for paw.
explain: Paw can also be a verb, a doing word. A dog pawing at the door is touching or scratching the door with its paw because it wants to go out. The words around the word show you which meaning is being used.
explain: Be careful with jokes. Paws can mean hands, as in «get your paws off», which is a silly way of saying "take your hands off". The sentence tells you which meaning to choose.
fact: A paw is the foot of an animal such as a cat, dog, bear or rabbit.
fact: Most paws have claws and soft pads.
fact: Paw can also be a verb, meaning to touch or scratch something with a paw.
fact: Paws is a jokey word for hands.
fact: Paws help animals walk, run, dig, climb and hold food, and the pads cushion each step.
exercise: «Your dog is fast asleep on the rug, but its paws are paddling.» What are paws? | *Feet of an animal | Bits of food | Sounds that a dog makes | Soft blankets on the rug
exercise: A dog is pawing at the door. What is it doing? | Sleeping against the door | *Touching or scratching the door with its paw | Barking loudly at a cat | Opening the door with a key
exercise: Mum says, «Get your paws off my cake!» What does paws mean in this joke? | Claws | Soft pads | *Hands | Feet of a cat
test: A rabbit was «cleaning his silly face with his paws», and «had to cuff his head once or twice». What does cuff mean? | Wash in water | Stroke gently | *Hit with an open paw | Dig a hole
test: Which part of an animal usually has claws and soft pads? | *Paw | Ear | Tail | Whisker
exam: Which sentence uses paw as a verb, meaning to touch or scratch with a paw? | Get your paws off my sandwich | The cat has four paws | Paws help animals climb trees | *The dog paws at the door to be let out
